e3310","html_url":"https://github.com/BlueCube3310","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-21T14:58:24Z","updated_at":"2026-08-21T14:58:24Z","body":"Most color textures with an alpha mask (even in HDR color space) tend to limit the alpha channel to the standard range of 0.0 - 1.0, which is what the algorithm here expects. \r\n\r\nI think it could be worth mentioning in the docs that this feature is intended mainly for color textures and that the alpha channel will be clamped to a range from 0.0 - 1.0","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5371562415/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5372604539","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104289#issuecomment-5372604539","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104289","id":5372604539,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQDtwew","user":{"login":"BlueCube3310","id":53150244,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTUwMjQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53150244?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310","html_url":"https://github.com/BlueCube3310","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-21T16:35:58Z","updated_at":"2026-08-21T16:35:58Z","body":"Inspired by [this article](https://lisyarus.github.io/blog/posts/exploring-ways-to-mipmap-alpha-tested-textures.html) [^1], I've made the following comparison to show the differences between some of the coverage options:\r\n\r\n| Setting | Alpha test |\r\n|---------|------------------|\r\n| No coverage |<img width=\"2635\" height=\"455\" alt=\"no_coverage\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7af941ab-fd97-4fe9-890c-c86f0a1b34c8\" />|\r\n| 50% coverage (default) | <img width=\"2209\" height=\"278\" alt=\"coverage_05\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6e5253cf-118b-43c5-90b5-fe7e1497a637\" /> |\r\n| 99% coverage (maximum) | <img width=\"2138\" height=\"256\" alt=\"coverage_099\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ad23407c-1248-48ba-ae6f-3ed5afd8d351\" />|\r\n\r\n[^1]: The author states that the coverage method still shrinks the alpha area, but they seem to be using a fixed alpha threshold of 50%. [This post](https://mastodon.gamedev.place/@castano/113785693026704816) suggests using an adjustable threshold and subsampling (both of which have been implemented in this PR).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5372604539/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":3,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5373326665","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104289#issuecomment-5373326665","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104289","id":5373326665,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQEZ1SQ","user":{"login":"Arnklit","id":4955051,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NTUwNTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4955051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit","html_url":"https://github.com/Arnklit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-21T17:48:27Z","updated_at":"2026-08-21T17:48:27Z","body":"> Most color textures with an alpha mask (even in HDR color space) tend to limit the alpha channel to the standard range of 0.0 - 1.0, which is what the algorithm here expects.\r\n> \r\n> I think it could be worth mentioning in the docs that this feature is intended mainly for color textures and that the alpha channel will be clamped to a range from 0.0 - 1.0\r\n\r\nThanks for clarifying that. I added the sentence at the end of the doc description. \"This option is intended for color textures and clamps the alpha channel in the 0.0 - 1.0 range.\" ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5373326665/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5396000146","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104289#issuecomment-5396000146","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104289","id":5396000146,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQaBtkg","user":{"login":"Arnklit","id":4955051,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NTUwNTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4955051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit","html_url":"https://github.com/Arnklit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-24T13:36:45Z","updated_at":"2026-08-24T13:36:45Z","body":"@Calinou would this be good to approve for merge at this point?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5396000146/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5400802915","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104289#issuecomment-5400802915","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104289","id":5400802915,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQem2Yw","user":{"login":"Arnklit","id":4955051,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NTUwNTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4955051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit","html_url":"https://github.com/Arnklit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arnklit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-24T20:16:35Z","updated_at":"2026-08-24T20:16:35Z","body":"> Code looks good to me.\r\n> \r\n> One remaining thing is to recommend the use of this import option in these descriptions:\r\n> \r\n> https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/bfae01d184c6168b55d48caefa19d5cda6c8ba10/doc/classes/BaseMaterial3D.xml#L587-L589\r\n> \r\n> https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/bfae01d184c6168b55d48caefa19d5cda6c8ba10/doc/classes/BaseMaterial3D.xml#L84-L86\r\n> with the `alpha_test_threshold` ideally set to match `alpha_scissor_threshold`.\r\n\r\nGreat! I'll see about adding that tomorrow :)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.c